# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite.
#
# ── Why every route is written out by hand ──────────────────────────────────
#
# NEVER add `/*  /  200`.
#
# Cloudflare's own documentation says it plainly: "Redirects are always
# followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request." A _redirects rule is evaluated BEFORE Pages looks for a file, so a
# catch-all does not merely cover unmatched paths — it shadows every real file
# on the site, including /assets/index-<hash>.js. And _headers marks /assets/*
# immutable for a year, so the edge would cache the HTML shell under a script
# URL and clients would get a blank page until somebody purged the cache. That
# is the 12.08.2026 outage exactly (infrastructure.md → "Deploy trap"), and a
# redeploy does not fix it.
#
# The obvious guard is unavailable: _redirects supports no non-3xx/200 status,
# so a `/assets/* … 404` rule cannot be placed in front of a catch-all.
# Enumeration is not a style preference, it is the only shape that works.
#
# public/404.html is the other half of this: everything NOT named below gets a
# real 404 rather than a 200 full of HTML.
#
# ── Why the destination is "/" and not "/index.html" ────────────────────────
#
# Measured on production, 12.09.2026. Cloudflare Pages normalises /index.html
# to / with a 308, and a rewrite whose destination is /index.html inherits that:
#   /games          -> 308, location: /      (static rule, normalised away)
#   /coachees/abc   -> 404                   (dynamic rule, did not resolve)
# so the 200 rewrite silently became a redirect for the exact routes, and
# nothing at all for the ones carrying an id. Rewriting to "/" serves the same
# shell without going through that normalisation.
#
# There is deliberately no /sign or /survey rule. Those two keep their token in
# the URL FRAGMENT, which is never sent to a server, so they are always served
# from "/" and no token-shaped path can reach an edge log even by accident.
# See src/lib/routes.ts → "Two transports, on purpose".

# ── exact app routes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/home            /            200
/coachees        /            200
/games           /            200
/calendar        /            200
/form            /            200
/feedbacks       /            200
/coachee-games   /            200
/admin           /            200
/guide           /            200
/demo            /            200

# ── dynamic ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stays first in this block: first match wins, and this one is more specific.
# The app used to live under the /svrz_rc/ subpath on GitHub Pages. Anyone who
# pastes an old link with the new host keeps working instead of hitting a 404.
# The #hash (survey and sign tokens live there) is preserved by the browser.
/svrz_rc/*       /:splat      301

/coachees/*      /            200
/games/*         /            200
/form/*          /            200
/feedbacks/*     /            200
/admin/*         /            200
/guide/*         /            200
